WEBVTT

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:16.160
Polar Bear's Café

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:20.450
Polar Bear's Café

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:34.940
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:33.970
Sales Penguin!

00:01:37.460 --> 00:01:39.160
So, Mr. Llama,

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:41.280
There's something that
 I've been wondering...

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:42.990
Yes?

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:44.530
How exactly do you...

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:48.290
...sit in a chair?

00:01:48.860 --> 00:01:51.450
I'd rather not hear that from you.

00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:55.460
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:01:56.470 --> 00:01:58.900
All right, let's start 
our sales meeting.

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:00.340
The subject is...

00:02:00.830 --> 00:02:02.520
in regard to a possible promotion

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:05.500
to help sell the overwhelming 
amount of leftover penguin cards.

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:10.740
We didn't have much luck during 
Christmas or New Year's, either.

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:14.020
I told you we didn't need to make so many.

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:17.960
We have a large percentage 
of Penguins today.

00:02:17.960 --> 00:02:19.320
Looks like it.

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:21.500
I guess it's because we're

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:23.000
right in the middle of our raw fish fair.

00:02:23.470 --> 00:02:24.990
That's not it.

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:27.680
I thought they would sell.

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:30.460
Jeez, all you have going 
for you is enthusiasm.

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:33.890
I wonder what the penguin cards are.

00:02:33.890 --> 00:02:35.560
They're cards of penguins.

00:02:36.440 --> 00:02:38.710
I guess you don't feel like explaining.

00:02:38.710 --> 00:02:39.490
Nope.

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:42.180
Anyway, we have to do something

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:43.930
with the stock we already have.

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:46.600
All right. Let's start 
throwing out ideas.

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:51.250
The penguins seem to be having 
an impassioned discussion.

00:02:51.250 --> 00:02:54.270
And then we have you,

00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:56.280
a penguin who's not very impassioned

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:58.850
and just sits there drinking his coffee.

00:02:58.850 --> 00:03:03.640
Could you not describe the free time 
 I treat myself to like that?

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:07.490
Ideas, huh...

00:03:07.490 --> 00:03:08.970
Hmm...

00:03:10.150 --> 00:03:11.500
Hello.

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:13.750
Oh, Mr. Panda.

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:16.760
Um, let's see, it was P—

00:03:16.760 --> 00:03:19.320
We're the genus Pygoscelis.

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:20.220
Ah.

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:23.830
I'm the lover of the South 
Pole, Adélie penguin.

00:03:24.380 --> 00:03:27.380
I'm stoic and modest, Chinstrap penguin.

00:03:27.950 --> 00:03:31.440
I have a stylish personality, 
Gentoo penguin.

00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:33.650
The three of us make up...

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:35.250
P—

00:03:36.510 --> 00:03:38.280
The three of us make up...

00:03:39.080 --> 00:03:40.030
P—

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:43.290
The Pygoscelis genus!

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:44.490
Ah.

00:03:45.010 --> 00:03:47.460
There's an easy way to remember it.

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:49.170
The "Pi" in pilates,

00:03:49.170 --> 00:03:51.450
the "Go" in Guovdageaidnu...

00:03:51.450 --> 00:03:53.480
You're actually making 
it harder to remember.

00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:55.970
What is that "Go" whatever anyways?

00:03:55.970 --> 00:03:57.990
It's a village in Norway, of course.

00:03:57.990 --> 00:03:59.300
"Of course"?

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:02.000
Would you not say it like 
I was supposed to know?

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:03.850
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin.

00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:05.440
What is it?

00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:07.470
That's rare coming 
from you, Miss Sasako.

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:10.630
There are so many Penguins today

00:04:10.630 --> 00:04:12.150
that it's a bit confusing.

00:04:12.730 --> 00:04:15.190
There aren't that many...

00:04:15.930 --> 00:04:18.360
Stay behind the counter.

00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:20.460
Uh...

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:23.320
You mean like this?

00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:27.030
Yep. Thanks.

00:04:27.950 --> 00:04:29.810
Is it really okay

00:04:29.810 --> 00:04:31.450
for me to be here?

00:04:34.760 --> 00:04:37.790
First of all, we have to figure 
out a way to play with these.

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:39.030
I know!

00:04:39.030 --> 00:04:40.000
Go ahead.

00:04:40.510 --> 00:04:42.870
How about making them 
like trading cards?

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:45.560
I hate to say this,

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:47.940
but there really isn't 
any point to trading them.

00:04:47.940 --> 00:04:49.970
There just aren't that many kinds.

00:04:50.750 --> 00:04:51.680
I know!

00:04:52.360 --> 00:04:53.850
You know how people give

00:04:53.850 --> 00:04:55.660
chocolates on Valentine's Day?

00:04:55.660 --> 00:04:56.400
Yeah.

00:04:56.910 --> 00:04:59.070
Why don't we make a day where people

00:04:59.070 --> 00:05:00.710
give penguin cards?

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:02.740
St. Penguin's Day.

00:05:03.410 --> 00:05:04.860
What do you think, Miss?

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:05.530
Huh?

00:05:07.220 --> 00:05:09.160
I don't think I'd want one.

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:11.620
A St. Penguin's Day?

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:14.510
Or the card in general.

00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:17.020
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:19.800
How can you say such a thing?!

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:22.010
How about you stop 
carrying around coffee

00:05:22.010 --> 00:05:24.190
and come up with ideas?!

00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:26.020
Me?

00:05:26.020 --> 00:05:27.740
Anything would be fine.

00:05:28.730 --> 00:05:30.380
The train station...

00:05:30.380 --> 00:05:32.020
Yes? What about the train station?

00:05:33.010 --> 00:05:34.700
How about giving them away

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:37.600
with tissues in front 
of the train station?

00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:39.240
<i>Here you go.</i>

00:05:40.270 --> 00:05:42.070
<i>Thank you for your patronage.</i>

00:05:42.520 --> 00:05:44.030
Hey, wait a minute!

00:05:44.030 --> 00:05:45.500
Are you saying that these cards

00:05:45.500 --> 00:05:47.180
are so worthless, they need to be

00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:48.510
handed out with tissues?!

00:05:49.140 --> 00:05:50.530
I'm sorry.

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:53.130
How about you add a handshake ticket,

00:05:53.130 --> 00:05:56.000
as well as a voting ticket 
for the Penguin election?

00:05:57.380 --> 00:06:00.470
That makes absolutely no sense.

00:06:00.470 --> 00:06:02.710
Oh, I know. If you fold the card...

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:06.850
They'd make great shoehorns.

00:06:07.350 --> 00:06:09.540
Definitely disposable shoehorns.

00:06:10.050 --> 00:06:11.390
Also...

00:06:13.370 --> 00:06:17.060
Kumada Commercial Banquet Hall

00:06:14.170 --> 00:06:17.060
Ooh, party tricks!

00:06:17.300 --> 00:06:18.340
What do you think?

00:06:18.930 --> 00:06:20.640
That's a great idea!

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:24.510
You guys can go back to work now.

00:06:26.550 --> 00:06:30.320
We'll now be continuing 
our sales meeting...

00:06:32.360 --> 00:06:34.920
I see that you're still here.

00:06:34.920 --> 00:06:38.310
Why do you have penguin cards, anyway?

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:41.500
Well, we wanted people to learn the

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:43.040
different types of penguins.

00:06:43.390 --> 00:06:46.260
You know! Many people love penguins,

00:06:46.260 --> 00:06:48.380
but when it comes to the 
types, they have no idea.

00:06:48.920 --> 00:06:52.870
Penguins have various 
appearances and personalities.

00:06:53.370 --> 00:06:56.020
All of them are completely different.

00:06:56.500 --> 00:06:58.480
Then can any of you fly?

00:06:59.690 --> 00:07:02.670
Well, we're all alike in that aspect....

00:07:03.180 --> 00:07:05.800
Some of us lay elliptical eggs,

00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:07.940
and some lay pear-shaped eggs.

00:07:06.760 --> 00:07:07.940
Yes, yes.

00:07:08.660 --> 00:07:10.650
Can they be about the same?

00:07:12.060 --> 00:07:13.620
No.

00:07:15.790 --> 00:07:18.580
Why don't you target little children?

00:07:25.610 --> 00:07:27.700
So, what do you think of this card?

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:33.040
All aboard!

00:07:33.040 --> 00:07:34.370
Aboard!

00:07:34.370 --> 00:07:36.450
They don't want to look at them today.

00:07:41.770 --> 00:07:44.510
There are lots of the same cards.

00:07:44.510 --> 00:07:46.770
No, they're all different.

00:07:47.330 --> 00:07:49.900
Are these two different species, too?

00:07:50.350 --> 00:07:53.050
This one is a Royal penguin,

00:07:53.050 --> 00:07:55.370
and this one is a Macaroni penguin.

00:07:55.940 --> 00:07:59.680
You can easily tell because the 
Royal penguins have white faces.

00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:04.790
These two are vaguely different.

00:08:05.340 --> 00:08:08.250
That is a Humboldt penguin 
and a Magellanic penguin.

00:08:08.790 --> 00:08:11.610
You can tell them apart

00:08:11.610 --> 00:08:13.220
by the stripe on their chest.

00:08:14.050 --> 00:08:16.270
Is there a reason to tell them apart?

00:08:16.770 --> 00:08:17.930
Of course there is!

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:21.160
It's a Humboldt penguin 
and a Magellanic penguin!

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:22.940
It's vague.

00:08:24.840 --> 00:08:25.960
What?

00:08:26.470 --> 00:08:28.210
Did you want to throw 
them away after all?

00:08:28.210 --> 00:08:31.060
No! Why would we throw them away?!

00:08:31.730 --> 00:08:33.110
I just got a great idea!

00:08:34.010 --> 00:08:36.320
How about playing Memory with them?

00:08:36.890 --> 00:08:39.030
Memory?

00:08:39.840 --> 00:08:42.670
You use two decks of Penguin cards,

00:08:42.670 --> 00:08:45.490
and if you get two of 
the same card, you win.

00:08:45.490 --> 00:08:47.800
Maybe that'll help 
people tell us apart.

00:08:47.800 --> 00:08:49.000
Good idea!

00:08:49.250 --> 00:08:50.500
Let's go with that!

00:08:51.310 --> 00:08:54.040
So you have to buy two decks?

00:08:55.640 --> 00:08:57.730
Yes, is there a problem?!

00:08:58.090 --> 00:09:00.970
I'd be reluctant to buy two decks.

00:09:01.370 --> 00:09:03.000
All right, fine!

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:04.980
We'll make it two for the price of one!

00:09:06.230 --> 00:09:08.310
Let's go ahead and give it a try.

00:09:09.850 --> 00:09:12.480
Wow, this looks fun.

00:09:12.810 --> 00:09:16.120
Now, Mr. Panda, pick a card.

00:09:16.120 --> 00:09:17.700
Let's see...

00:09:18.190 --> 00:09:19.910
The first one is...

00:09:20.480 --> 00:09:22.120
The Emperor.

00:09:22.780 --> 00:09:24.580
And the second one is...

00:09:25.320 --> 00:09:26.250
This one.

00:09:27.490 --> 00:09:29.570
Oh! I got a mat—

00:09:31.160 --> 00:09:33.960
Stare...

00:09:34.490 --> 00:09:35.690
Or not.

00:09:35.690 --> 00:09:37.770
They're totally different.

00:09:37.770 --> 00:09:39.680
The second one was the King.

00:09:39.940 --> 00:09:42.170
I think if you look at 
the patterns and size,

00:09:42.170 --> 00:09:44.520
you can tell them apart more easily.

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:45.820
Please look at the patterns...

00:09:45.820 --> 00:09:48.400
...and the difference in size.

00:09:57.730 --> 00:10:00.560
Oh! This time I got a match!

00:10:00.990 --> 00:10:02.330
Yay!

00:10:03.060 --> 00:10:04.170
So close!

00:10:04.170 --> 00:10:07.330
That's a Snares penguin 
and a Fiordland penguin.

00:10:07.880 --> 00:10:10.430
Those two do look rather similar, 
so they are easy to mistake.

00:10:11.380 --> 00:10:13.820
I got a match!

00:10:13.820 --> 00:10:16.720
That's a Cape penguin 
and a Galapagos penguin.

00:10:17.610 --> 00:10:19.970
Truly very close.

00:10:21.190 --> 00:10:24.390
That's a Rockhopper penguin 
and an Erect-crested penguin.

00:10:25.400 --> 00:10:27.850
So close! You've almost got it!

00:10:29.910 --> 00:10:32.590
Is this really fun?

00:10:32.590 --> 00:10:34.620
Of course it's fun!

00:10:34.620 --> 00:10:36.360
Come on, keep playing!

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:39.140
I don't wanna play anymore.

00:10:39.140 --> 00:10:42.140
There was a Yellow-eyed penguin 
somewhere, wasn't there?

00:10:43.620 --> 00:10:45.840
Wasn't it somewhere around here?

00:10:45.840 --> 00:10:47.190
Oh, too bad.

00:10:47.190 --> 00:10:49.040
Now it's my turn.

00:10:49.810 --> 00:10:53.440
I got a Little penguin 
and a Rockhopper penguin.

00:10:53.440 --> 00:10:54.640
Too bad.

00:10:54.640 --> 00:10:56.620
All right, it's my turn.

00:10:56.620 --> 00:10:57.940
They're having fun!

00:10:57.940 --> 00:10:59.010
This could work!

00:10:59.010 --> 00:11:00.180
We did it!

00:11:00.180 --> 00:11:02.230
All right! Let's go with this.

00:11:03.140 --> 00:11:05.970
We're going to go sell now.

00:11:07.850 --> 00:11:09.980
Thank you very much.

00:11:09.980 --> 00:11:12.350
These are hard to tell apart.

00:11:13.570 --> 00:11:16.180
But that's what makes it fun.

00:11:16.900 --> 00:11:18.900
This is a game for grown-ups.

00:11:19.200 --> 00:11:22.810
It's hard to tell them apart, 
so you can play for hours.

00:11:22.810 --> 00:11:25.810
With extra emphasis on the hard part.

00:11:25.810 --> 00:11:29.870
I wonder how good 
of a game that would be.

00:11:30.640 --> 00:11:32.620
Panda, Panda.

00:11:32.620 --> 00:11:35.590
Is it okay if I come out now?

00:11:35.890 --> 00:11:40.020
Oh! Where were you, Mr. Penguin?

00:11:40.020 --> 00:11:43.550
Don't just stand there. Come join us!

00:11:44.900 --> 00:11:48.290
Well, I appreciate the offer,

00:11:48.290 --> 00:11:50.070
but the reason I came over here

00:11:50.070 --> 00:11:51.980
is because you told to.

00:11:52.500 --> 00:11:53.960
I guess there's no point 
in bringing it up.

00:11:53.960 --> 00:11:55.010
Beep, beep!

00:11:55.010 --> 00:11:58.530
We are arriving! We are arriving!

00:11:58.810 --> 00:12:01.280
All aboard!

00:12:02.630 --> 00:12:04.270
Do you want another café mocha?

00:12:05.110 --> 00:12:06.750
I think I do.

00:12:08.950 --> 00:12:13.920
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:12:10.010 --> 00:12:12.920
Mr. Penguin's Picnic.

00:12:16.700 --> 00:12:18.300
Welcome.

00:12:21.600 --> 00:12:24.510
Would you like your usual, Mr. Penguin?

00:12:26.240 --> 00:12:27.530
Whatever's fine.

00:12:28.860 --> 00:12:30.810
Whatever?

00:12:31.330 --> 00:12:34.010
Then I'll totally bring 
out something amazing!

00:12:34.010 --> 00:12:35.400
Please don't.

00:12:38.230 --> 00:12:39.730
What's the matter?

00:12:40.320 --> 00:12:41.820
Picnic.

00:12:42.340 --> 00:12:43.670
Picnic?

00:12:44.630 --> 00:12:48.910
Do you want to go on a picnic 
tomorrow, Polar Bear?

00:12:48.910 --> 00:12:52.770
Sorry, I have plans to go 
mini golfing tomorrow.

00:12:53.150 --> 00:12:55.250
How about you, Miss Sasako?

00:12:55.250 --> 00:12:56.590
Tomorrow?

00:12:57.420 --> 00:12:59.000
I have to work here.

00:12:59.610 --> 00:13:01.110
I see...

00:13:02.310 --> 00:13:03.910
Hello.

00:13:05.120 --> 00:13:06.300
Panda!

00:13:06.300 --> 00:13:07.180
What?

00:13:07.180 --> 00:13:09.360
Just say yes!

00:13:09.360 --> 00:13:11.140
What are you talking about?

00:13:11.140 --> 00:13:13.560
It doesn't matter. Just say yes!

00:13:13.560 --> 00:13:16.400
I've done tons of ridiculous 
things for you!

00:13:16.400 --> 00:13:18.110
What?

00:13:18.590 --> 00:13:22.670
I can't say "yes" so suddenly.

00:13:23.150 --> 00:13:25.320
Is this really where 
you get embarrassed?

00:13:27.770 --> 00:13:29.370
What am I going to do?

00:13:30.400 --> 00:13:31.600
What's wrong?

00:13:31.600 --> 00:13:33.330
You see...

00:13:34.410 --> 00:13:38.810
I've been chased by the 
Penkos all this time...

00:13:35.780 --> 00:13:37.470
Mr. Penguin!

00:13:38.930 --> 00:13:40.790
Wait up!

00:13:39.210 --> 00:13:40.790
The other day...

00:13:42.510 --> 00:13:43.760
So...

00:13:44.280 --> 00:13:45.930
Who do you really like?

00:13:57.130 --> 00:13:59.770
They've really got you in a corner.

00:14:00.340 --> 00:14:01.920
It's true.

00:14:01.920 --> 00:14:05.090
I've never had such a 
tasteless coffee in my life.

00:14:05.090 --> 00:14:06.940
I can imagine.

00:14:06.940 --> 00:14:10.490
So, Mr. Penguin, how did you answer?

00:14:11.330 --> 00:14:12.410
Well...

00:14:31.780 --> 00:14:34.640
I like you all! I can't choose!

00:14:34.640 --> 00:14:36.570
I like you all!

00:14:38.860 --> 00:14:41.260
That's pretty awful, Mr. Penguin.

00:14:43.050 --> 00:14:47.670
But there's nothing else I could 
have said in that situation.

00:14:47.670 --> 00:14:49.840
So what happened after that?

00:14:50.460 --> 00:14:52.590
So now we're going out.

00:14:52.590 --> 00:14:53.950
With which one?

00:14:54.330 --> 00:14:56.200
With all of them.

00:14:56.720 --> 00:14:58.160
What?

00:14:58.840 --> 00:15:00.770
That's my line.

00:15:00.770 --> 00:15:02.630
It's terrible.

00:15:03.450 --> 00:15:08.030
Because I have to date all 
seven of them equally.

00:15:09.110 --> 00:15:11.840
That does sound rather difficult.

00:15:12.130 --> 00:15:14.760
Yeah, it's hard but...

00:15:16.050 --> 00:15:18.230
The hardest part is...

00:15:19.000 --> 00:15:20.760
Oh yeah, Miss Penko...

00:15:22.140 --> 00:15:24.650
What? I'm Penjolina!

00:15:24.890 --> 00:15:26.300
S-Sorry!

00:15:26.900 --> 00:15:28.590
Um, Miss Penko?

00:15:29.900 --> 00:15:31.570
I'm Penna!

00:15:32.700 --> 00:15:35.530
Um, Miss Penko is...

00:15:37.750 --> 00:15:40.630
I can't tell the seven of them apart!

00:15:41.770 --> 00:15:43.280
It must be hard.

00:15:43.910 --> 00:15:45.350
It is hard.

00:15:45.760 --> 00:15:49.470
I can't put their faces with their names, 
no matter how hard I try.

00:15:50.120 --> 00:15:51.960
How rude!

00:15:52.490 --> 00:15:54.720
You should at least remember our names!

00:15:55.340 --> 00:15:58.750
You always said how much you liked them,

00:15:58.750 --> 00:16:00.630
and you still don't remember their faces?

00:16:01.120 --> 00:16:04.080
I think liking them, and being 
able to tell them apart

00:16:04.080 --> 00:16:05.740
are two different things.

00:16:05.740 --> 00:16:08.690
There's a flaw in that 
reasoning somewhere.

00:16:09.340 --> 00:16:11.370
What should I do?

00:16:11.370 --> 00:16:14.410
Not to mention, I have to 
go on a picnic tomorrow!

00:16:14.820 --> 00:16:17.080
All by your lonesome?

00:16:17.080 --> 00:16:18.840
Of course not!

00:16:18.840 --> 00:16:20.100
Can't you see the flow here?

00:16:20.100 --> 00:16:21.870
I'm going with the Penkos!

00:16:21.870 --> 00:16:23.870
It'll be very lively!

00:16:24.370 --> 00:16:27.070
Can someone go with me

00:16:27.070 --> 00:16:30.750
and whisper in my ear who's who?

00:16:30.750 --> 00:16:33.260
Like the owner of a traditional 
Japanese restaurant would.

00:16:33.660 --> 00:16:35.990
Who might you be referring to?

00:16:35.990 --> 00:16:38.060
All right. I'll go.

00:16:38.320 --> 00:16:39.970
What? Really?!

00:16:40.530 --> 00:16:42.430
All right! I'll do my best.

00:16:43.410 --> 00:16:45.300
On second thought, don't come.

00:16:47.420 --> 00:16:48.980
What should I do?

00:16:49.580 --> 00:16:52.250
How can I remember them all?

00:16:52.250 --> 00:16:54.720
Why don't you have them wear name tags?

00:16:54.720 --> 00:16:58.950
I can't ask a lady to pin 
a name tag on her chest.

00:16:58.950 --> 00:17:00.580
That wouldn't be very good.

00:17:01.290 --> 00:17:02.900
I know!

00:17:02.900 --> 00:17:03.710
What?

00:17:04.160 --> 00:17:07.520
Why don't you have the Penkos

00:17:07.520 --> 00:17:10.010
say their names before speaking?

00:17:13.460 --> 00:17:15.950
<i>Hi! I'm Penno!</i>

00:17:16.540 --> 00:17:18.350
<i>How about we have lunch now?</i>

00:17:19.340 --> 00:17:21.490
<i>Sounds great, Penno.</i>

00:17:22.510 --> 00:17:25.030
<i>Hi! I'm Penjolina!</i>

00:17:25.370 --> 00:17:26.770
<i>Would you like some tea?</i>

00:17:27.720 --> 00:17:30.190
<i>Thank you, Penjolina.</i>

00:17:31.340 --> 00:17:33.990
I like it! That system is great!

00:17:34.810 --> 00:17:36.660
But there's a flaw.

00:17:36.660 --> 00:17:40.020
Would you really be able 
to ask them to do that?

00:17:40.420 --> 00:17:42.580
I wonder how I should go 
about asking them.

00:17:43.250 --> 00:17:45.260
That's easy!

00:17:45.260 --> 00:17:49.320
Just say you can't tell them apart
 and then ask them for their names.

00:17:49.320 --> 00:17:52.550
If I actually said that, 
I'd be in a lot of trouble!

00:17:52.550 --> 00:17:54.450
I'll tell them for you.

00:17:55.550 --> 00:17:58.000
I'm Miss Polar Bear.

00:17:58.700 --> 00:18:02.090
There's no point in you naming yourself!

00:18:02.610 --> 00:18:04.620
Oh, how about this?

00:18:04.620 --> 00:18:05.390
What?

00:18:05.970 --> 00:18:09.130
How about you have
each of the Penkos

00:18:09.130 --> 00:18:11.860
wear a different colored ribbon?

00:18:12.560 --> 00:18:14.650
If they each have a color,

00:18:14.650 --> 00:18:16.050
wouldn't it be easier to remember them?

00:18:16.470 --> 00:18:17.460
<i>Penko.</i>

00:18:18.550 --> 00:18:19.780
<i>Penmi.</i>

00:18:20.420 --> 00:18:24.040
See? Wouldn't you be able 
to tell them apart then?

00:18:24.300 --> 00:18:25.250
That's it!

00:18:25.760 --> 00:18:27.750
Then I can remember them!

00:18:28.210 --> 00:18:30.170
Thank you, Miss Sasako!

00:18:30.170 --> 00:18:32.380
I'd like to give you 
the Nobel Ribbon Award!

00:18:32.380 --> 00:18:34.090
Thanks, guys!

00:18:34.090 --> 00:18:35.670
I'm going home now.

00:18:36.110 --> 00:18:38.400
I'm going to do my best 
to remember their names!

00:18:38.400 --> 00:18:39.470
See ya!

00:18:42.100 --> 00:18:44.080
Not only could he not 
tell their faces apart,

00:18:44.080 --> 00:18:48.050
but apparently he still doesn't 
know all their names yet.

00:18:48.840 --> 00:18:49.810
Seems so.

00:18:50.480 --> 00:18:53.440
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:18:56.370 --> 00:19:00.910
Will you work for me 
tomorrow, Miss Sasako?

00:19:01.320 --> 00:19:02.840
You want me

00:19:02.840 --> 00:19:06.150
to go to the zoo in your place?

00:19:06.150 --> 00:19:08.470
You don't have to worry about the café.

00:19:08.470 --> 00:19:10.140
I'll be here.

00:19:10.140 --> 00:19:12.840
I don't think that's the issue.

00:19:14.320 --> 00:19:17.470
Just thinking about how troublesome 
work will be tomorrow

00:19:17.470 --> 00:19:20.380
has made me too exhausted to move today.

00:19:20.380 --> 00:19:21.830
Wow...

00:19:22.340 --> 00:19:25.670
By the way, I'm curious how Mr. Penguin's

00:19:25.670 --> 00:19:27.460
picnic went yesterday.

00:19:35.310 --> 00:19:36.500
Are you okay?

00:19:36.930 --> 00:19:39.320
How did your ribbon strategy go?

00:19:39.780 --> 00:19:42.070
Well, you see...

00:19:42.770 --> 00:19:46.790
I have a present for all of you!

00:19:47.060 --> 00:19:49.790
Oh, how cute!

00:19:50.340 --> 00:19:52.250
Here you go, Penko.

00:19:54.460 --> 00:19:55.920
Thank you.

00:19:56.580 --> 00:19:58.420
Here you go, Penna.

00:19:59.160 --> 00:20:00.370
Thank you.

00:20:00.800 --> 00:20:02.630
Oh, how pretty!

00:20:02.630 --> 00:20:04.100
Look! Look!

00:20:02.940 --> 00:20:04.130
Penmi.

00:20:04.100 --> 00:20:07.560
It'll totally look good on you!

00:20:04.770 --> 00:20:05.850
Thank you.

00:20:05.850 --> 00:20:07.560
I'm so happy.

00:20:08.720 --> 00:20:12.020
I made sure to remember 
which name matched which color.

00:20:12.740 --> 00:20:14.830
That's great.

00:20:14.830 --> 00:20:17.500
Good job, Mr. Penguin.

00:20:17.910 --> 00:20:19.530
But then...

00:20:20.520 --> 00:20:24.190
Come on, Penjolina and Penka! 
You can do it!

00:20:24.620 --> 00:20:25.590
Okay!

00:20:26.610 --> 00:20:30.580
You're almost there, Penno and Penuelle!

00:20:30.580 --> 00:20:31.530
Okay!

00:20:32.080 --> 00:20:34.130
Sounds like it went well.

00:20:34.130 --> 00:20:35.960
To this point.

00:20:36.570 --> 00:20:38.150
We all made it together.

00:20:38.150 --> 00:20:40.790
Wow! It looks delicious!

00:20:41.860 --> 00:20:43.720
I'm so happy!

00:20:43.720 --> 00:20:46.140
Oh, Mr. Penguin!

00:20:46.860 --> 00:20:49.560
Could you get me a riceball, Penna?

00:20:50.150 --> 00:20:53.270
What? I'm Penko.

00:20:53.550 --> 00:20:57.270
What? But Penko should be...

00:20:58.280 --> 00:20:59.250
You, right?

00:20:59.950 --> 00:21:02.170
What? I'm Penmi!

00:21:02.170 --> 00:21:04.240
What? Why?!

00:21:04.550 --> 00:21:07.750
We liked these colors 
better, so we traded.

00:21:07.750 --> 00:21:09.410
Right?

00:21:09.410 --> 00:21:11.090
Look, look!

00:21:11.090 --> 00:21:12.550
Wait a minute!

00:21:12.550 --> 00:21:14.370
Why would you trade?!

00:21:14.370 --> 00:21:16.380
I'm telling you apart by 
the color of your ribbons!

00:21:16.380 --> 00:21:18.670
Now I won't know who is who!

00:21:24.560 --> 00:21:26.840
Oh! Uh, I-I mean...

00:21:26.270 --> 00:21:27.890
Mr. Penguin.

00:21:31.780 --> 00:21:33.750
So that's how it is.

00:21:36.400 --> 00:21:38.270
Let's all calm down.

00:21:44.570 --> 00:21:46.340
Ow, ow, ow...

00:21:56.570 --> 00:21:59.340
Stop! Stop! Stop!

00:22:05.020 --> 00:22:07.070
I see...

00:22:07.070 --> 00:22:09.320
I see your plan failed.

00:22:09.320 --> 00:22:11.680
Jeez, you guys.

00:22:12.290 --> 00:22:17.440
Couldn't you give me a better 
idea that I can actually use?

00:22:18.450 --> 00:22:21.680
How about you actually learn 
their names and faces?

00:22:21.680 --> 00:22:23.320
Yes, yes.

00:23:54.870 --> 00:24:25.290
Next Time

00:24:22.060 --> 00:24:24.440
Mr. Handa's Discussion
Panda Mama's Daily Life
